\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Which part of hardening matters (C11, C12; harden and rigid from C07, same seeds, settings and budget). Each cell $a:b$ counts the instances on which the first method\textquotesingle s lowest size is lower than the second\textquotesingle s, and the reverse; the rest are ties. \emph  {snap} compresses disks as hardening does, then switches to polygons at once; \emph  {grow-area} keeps rigid polygons whose area follows hardening\textquotesingle s.}}{11}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ablate}{{6}{11}{Which part of hardening matters (C11, C12; harden and rigid from C07, same seeds, settings and budget). Each cell $a:b$ counts the instances on which the first method\textquotesingle s lowest size is lower than the second\textquotesingle s, and the reverse; the rest are ties. \emph {snap} compresses disks as hardening does, then switches to polygons at once; \emph {grow-area} keeps rigid polygons whose area follows hardening\textquotesingle s}{table.6}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces What pieces do after compression, on the best run of each C07 instance with $n\ge 6$ (orange: hardening; blue: rigid; large dots: the method alone reached the lowest size). Left: mean net displacement; middle: mean net rotation, modulo the piece's symmetry (for hardening this includes turning while pieces are still nearly round and orientation costs almost nothing); right: share of pieces with no edge within $2^\circ $ of a container edge (square and triangle containers).}}{11}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mechanism}{{4}{11}{What pieces do after compression, on the best run of each C07 instance with $n\ge 6$ (orange: hardening; blue: rigid; large dots: the method alone reached the lowest size). Left: mean net displacement; middle: mean net rotation, modulo the piece's symmetry (for hardening this includes turning while pieces are still nearly round and orientation costs almost nothing); right: share of pieces with no edge within $2^\circ $ of a container edge (square and triangle containers)}{figure.4}{}}
